 8. Run `./vm.sh collect <machine> /absolute/new-results-directory`. It mounts
    only that stopped machine's results image, read-only, copies the files,
    and detaches it. The destination must be new and outside the pool storage.
+   Every copied file is hashed against its source on the mount, and the hashes
+   go to `COLLECT-MANIFEST.sha256` in the destination; check later with
+   `shasum -a 256 -c COLLECT-MANIFEST.sha256`. Exit 0 means every file copied
+   and matched; any other exit lists what did not. (Before 2026-09-24 collect
+   exited 1 with "Operation not permitted" while the files were intact: AROS
+   sets FAT's archive bit, macOS maps it to the super-user flag `SF_ARCHIVED`,
+   and copying file flags failed. Collect no longer copies flags.)
 9. Run `./vm.sh release <machine>` while stopped. Release preserves the guest
    installation, dependencies, settings and results. A reused machine is not
    a clean installation; record your changes and use unique result names.
