+### Audio
+
+`"audio"` decides where a guest's sound goes - pool-wide, or per machine under
+`machines.<name>.audio`, which wins:
+
+| value | guest hardware | where the sound goes |
+|---|---|---|
+| `none` | **no sound card at all** | nowhere. The default when the key is absent - what every machine had until 2026-09-24 |
+| `wav` | AC97 | recorded to `vm-pool-data/machines/<name>/audio.wav`, **overwritten at every start**. Nothing reaches the speakers |
+| `coreaudio` | AC97 | the host's speakers, live |
+
+**Set to `wav` pool-wide on 2026-09-24.** Chosen because the pool is headless
+and shared: a recording can be checked by an agent, and five machines do not
+play into the speakers at once. To listen live, stop that machine and set its
+own `audio` to `coreaudio`. Silence from a `wav` machine is expected - check the
+file, not the speakers.
+
+Validated on 2026-09-24: `v1-1` boots with the card, and mainline AROS lists
+`ac97.audio` in `DEVS:AHI`. A 3-second 440 Hz tone played with
+`SYS:Utilities/MultiView` (double-click the waveform to play) put real samples
+into `audio.wav` (44.1 kHz stereo 16-bit).
+
+**Known problems, not yet solved:**
+
+- only about 50 ms of the 3-second tone reached the file (9,536 bytes where
+  about 530 KB were due). Whether the guest's AHI stops early, the AC97
+  emulation starves under TCG, or the `wav` backend drops data is not known;
+- the file's RIFF and data sizes stayed 0 after `vm.sh stop`, so ordinary WAV
+  readers refuse it. The samples start at byte 44 and can be read as raw
+  44.1 kHz stereo signed 16-bit;
+- **v11: the guest's AHI units start on VOID** (checked 2026-09-24). With the
+  card present and `coreaudio` verified end to end, nothing was heard until
+  the AHI units were pointed at the card. Set it with `AROS:Prefs/AHI`: the
+  cycle gadget at the top selects the unit (`Music unit`, `Unit 0`..`Unit 3`),
+  the list below selects that unit's mode. Choose `ac97:16 bit stereo++` for
+  **both** `Music unit` and **`Unit 0`**, then **Save** (writes
+  `ENVARC:Sys/ahi.prefs`, which survives restarts). The prefs' own test sound
+  plays through the selected unit, so it can succeed on `Music unit` while
+  `Unit 0` is still silent. Programs using OpenAL (OpenLoco among them) open
+  `ahi.device` unit 0 (`AHI_DEFAULT_UNIT`), not the music unit. Beware the
+  modes named `Unit 0:...`: they belong to `device.audio` and forward *to*
+  unit 0 - they are not the unit selector.
+  Done on `v11-1` only so far (its `ahi.prefs` is saved); the other v11 slots
+  and both v1 slots still need it. An earlier note here said the install had
+  no AHI preferences program: wrong - it is `AROS:Prefs/AHI`;
+- QEMU logs `Can not open 'ac97.pi'` and `'ac97.mc'` (no host audio driver) at
+  every start with a sound card: those are the card's recording and microphone
+  inputs. The output voice is not in those messages.
+
+Growth: at 44.1 kHz stereo 16-bit a machine playing continuously writes about
+10 MB a minute to its `audio.wav`.
+
 This implementation uses macOS, Python 3, QEMU and the existing `hdiutil` image
 tools. It adds no service. Copy `tools/vm_pool.example.json` to the ignored
 `tools/vm_pool.local.json`, or point `AROS_VM_POOL_CONFIG` at a local file.
